## Background and Motivation

I'm currently working on adding union support to a custom serializer I've created. To do this, I need to know all of the type cases for a union, whether they're defined using public constructors or a `IUnionMembers` interface. However, I'm thinking it would be nice to have that defined within Roslyn itself.

I noticed there's a `UnionCaseTypes()` method but it's currently `internal` (https://source.dot.net/#Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp/Symbols/[NamedTypeSymbol.cs](https://source.dot.net/#Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp/Symbols/NamedTypeSymbol.cs,ce376ba63dd79b0e),ce376ba63dd79b0e). It **seems** like this would fill the need, but not sure if this is the "right" one to make public or another route should be taken.

## Proposed API

Something akin to the `UnionCaseTypes()` shown in the link mentioned above, though that method takes one parameter: `ref CompoundUseSiteInfo<AssemblySymbol> useSiteInfo` - I'm guessing that wouldn't be desirable to require a user to pass in. It may be better to have this as a read-only property of `INamedTypeSymbol` that returns a `ImmutableArray<INamedTypeSymbol>` instance (empty if the type is not a union).

## Usage Examples

```C#
// Assume myTypeSymbol is a valid INamedTypeSymbol

foreach (var unionCaseType in myTypeSymbol.UnionCaseTypes)
{
  // Use the case type as needed.
}
```

